        "subject": "LU-15096 ptlrpc: return the error when a reply cannot be sent",
        "message": "LU-15096 ptlrpc: return the error when a reply cannot be sent\n\nptl_send_buf() treated any LNetMDBind() failure as a transient\nout-of-memory and assumed that the error was -ENOMEM.  LNetMDBind()\ncould return other errors as well.  Return the actual error code.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I43731cf83647c12fe4ad71d9d3606590a33ebbe5\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/70339\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Marc Vef <mvef@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Yang Sheng <ys@whamcloud.com>\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Bruno Faccini <bfaccini@nvidia.com>\nReviewed-by: bzzztomas77 <azhuravlev@thelustrecollective.com>\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\n"
